Consider the following Kafka producer code snippet:

```java
KafkaProducer<String, String> producer = new KafkaProducer<>(props);
try {
    producer.send(new ProducerRecord<String, String>(
        "my-topic", "key", "value"),
        new Callback() {
            public void onCompletion(RecordMetadata metadata, Exception e) {
                if (e != null) {
                    e.printStackTrace();
                } else {
                    System.out.println("Sent successfully to partition " + 
                                     metadata.partition() + " at offset " + 
                                     metadata.offset());
                }
            }
        }
    );
} finally {
    producer.close();
}
```

When is the Callback's onCompletion method triggered?

